    "created_at": "2017-07-19T11:40:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-07-19T11:40:12Z",
    "body": "I think the \"create a DOMMatrix from a dictionary\" is meant to be generic and allow any unrestricted double values into the DOMMatrix.\r\n\r\nThe question is whether we want to disallow setting the current transform matrix to one that contains infinite/NaN values, or not. Probably yes, given how other functions seem to try to preserve this invariant, although I defer to experts like @whatwg/canvas.\r\n\r\n(Another question is, if we do want to reject it, whether we go with \"abort these steps\" for consistency, or throwing an error for fail-fast.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
