    "created_at": "2017-08-15T13:40:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-08-15T13:40:21Z",
    "body": "`DOMMatrix` itself intentionally preserves NaNs, I believe that was the preference from implementors from discussion a few years ago. But APIs that take a DOMMatrixInit as input can do something else. Let me know if there should be a variant of \"validate and fixup\" that throws if there are any non-finite values, or some such.",
